# Project Structure

Single module (`:app`). Package root is the app namespace (`<namespace>`).

```
<namespace>/
├── MainApplication.kt          // theme + locale restore, app-wide init
├── common/                     // app-wide, feature-independent
│   ├── firebase/               // EventsProvider, FirebaseUtils, RemoteConfiguration, RemoteConstants
│   ├── network/                // InternetManager
│   ├── observers/              // SingleLiveEvent
│   ├── permissions/
│   ├── repository/             // repositories shared by several features
│   └── viewmodel/              // ViewModels shared by several features
├── helpers/                    // stateless Kotlin extensions, grouped by concern
│   ├── constants/  datetime/  handlers/  lifecycle/  listener/  locale/
│   ├── menu/  navigation/  permissions/  settings/  theme/  ui/  utils/
├── presentation/
│   ├── MainActivity.kt
│   ├── base/                   // BaseActivity, BaseFragment, InsetsMode
│   ├── dialogs/                // reusable dialogs + dialogs/base builders
│   ├── startup/                // splash + onboarding
│   ├── home/
│   └── <feature>/              // one package per feature
└── storage/
    ├── preferences/            // SharedPrefManager
    └── provider/               // static/bundled data providers
```

## Feature Package

```
presentation/<feature>/
    Fragment<Feature>.kt
    <Feature>ViewModel.kt       // when the screen holds state
    adapters/
    interfaces/
    models/
    repository/
```

## Rules

- Keep related files together; prefer feature-based organisation over type-based.
- A helper used by two or more features moves to `helpers/` or `common/`.
- Reuse existing utilities before creating new ones. Search `helpers/` first.
- Never create a second helper that duplicates an existing one (toast, dialog, navigation, permission, date, screen size, image loading are all already covered).
- Never rename or move existing packages while implementing a feature.
- Avoid giant classes; split adapters, mappers and dialogs into their own files.
- Keep naming consistent with the existing files around you.

## Resources

```
res/
├── color/          // state selectors (ColorStateList)
├── drawable/       // bg_*, ic_*, flag_*
├── layout/         // activity_*, fragment_*, item_*, dialog_*
├── navigation/     // *_nav_graph.xml
├── values/         // colors, strings, themes, splash, urls, dimens
├── values-night/   // dark theme colour overrides
└── values-<lang>/  // localized strings
```
